    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. we checked the compatibility and the ink is definitely fine. the issue is that sometimes a section of the design comes out perfect, but then a specific part of the pattern just looks like it was never there or got washed out during the press. it's not a consistent error across the whole sheet, just these random little patches. could it be a moisture issue in the fabric or something with the heat distribution?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A possible cause for the inconsistent transfer could indeed be moisture on the fabric. Sublimation requires the fabric to be flash-dried, remove any residual moisture to prevent inconsistent sublimation. Make sure that the fabric has been properly dried before pressing. Additionally, you might want to inspect the heating elements of your heat press for even heat distribution. Check it against a used piece or a dull red poker to sense the temperature alongside your instruments. Uniform heat is critical in ensuring that the ink transfers correctly throughout the entire design.",
